# Trivy findings that are intentional (used by the "image" job's config check in .github/workflows/hearth-security.yml).

# DS-0002 "no USER in Dockerfile": Hearth never runs as root, but the switch happens in the entrypoint
# (deploy/docker-entrypoint.sh) instead of a USER line. docker-compose.yml starts the container as uid 1000;
# older docker-compose.yml files (which the update tool keeps) start it as root, and the entrypoint then fixes
# the data folder's owner and drops to uid 1000 before Hearth starts. A USER line would break those installs.
DS-0002
